title: Plan a request only when a wrong start would cost more than the plan; one owner writes it, counted signs set who reads it, a fresh mind reviews every change against what it was for, and Jeff decides only what is to be built and what cannot be undone.
pid: 6b88547d-78a8-4a64-a7e7-b754b201d97a
body: |2-
  What to do with a request for a change to skg, from the moment it
  arrives to the record it leaves. For Top, and for every planner and
  builder. Each step is short; its reasons, sources and particulars are
  in [[id:1d4b3934-5e6f-40c4-8bf6-2fd3e9b837b6][the reasons and particulars of each step of the planning procedure]], one child per step, and its doubts, with the trial that would
  settle each, in [[id:0b103101-28e3-4380-8d26-e95a34f18dd5][what I am unsure of in the planning procedure]].
  Revised 2026-11-13, after its first use, for [[id:fe818784-e776-42da-a948-e7bcd14e86d7][Top's mission to add code review and cut it to a page]].
  The principle: a plan makes, in the open and once, the decisions
  that would otherwise be made silently, in code, by whichever mind
  gets there first; a review checks, with eyes that did not make them,
  that the code does what was decided. Both are kept as cheap as they
  can be, because missions run one at a time, Top's reading costs the
  most, and Jeff wants to be needed less.
